WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
Scientists say that about
13.8 billion years ago,

2
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.910
the universe was extremely hot and dense.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.420
It has been expanding ever since.

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:15.670
The first person to propose this theory
was a Belgian physicist, Georges Lemaître.

5
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.250
He was also a Catholic priest.

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.550
So if the universe began with a Big Bang,

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.110
is there still room for a Creator?

8
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.150
In this mission, you'll
read the opening of Genesis,

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.590
and see why Christians read
it in very different ways.

10
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:35.900
Then you'll weigh up a bold claim: that
science has shown God did not create the

11
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.060
universe.

12
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.940
Your mission: find out whether a universe
that began with a Big Bang leaves room

13
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.150
for a Creator.
